WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.438
The best local model is not universal.

2
00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:11.809
Model choice should follow the task, the data sensitivity, the hardware available, the expected output format, and the level of review required.

3
00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:20.798
A model that is strong for brainstorming may not be the best choice for structured extraction, code assistance, or careful policy drafting.

4
00:00:20.798 --> 00:00:31.693
Hardware fit is central. Local model performance depends on available memory, accelerator support where present, CPU speed, storage performance, and context length.

5
00:00:31.693 --> 00:00:39.463
If the model does not fit the machine well, the user experience may be slow, unstable, or too constrained for the workflow.

6
00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:44.415
Quantized models can make local use more practical by reducing memory needs.

7
00:00:44.415 --> 00:00:49.063
That tradeoff may change speed, output quality, or reasoning behavior.

8
00:00:49.063 --> 00:00:53.024
The right question is not whether quantization is good or bad.

9
00:00:53.024 --> 00:00:59.576
The question is whether the model configuration meets the workflow's quality and reliability needs.

10
00:00:59.576 --> 00:01:07.042
Smaller models can be excellent for drafts, routing, simple transformations, study help, and routine assistance.

11
00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:14.127
Larger models may help with deeper reasoning or more complex synthesis when the local hardware supports them.

12
00:01:14.127 --> 00:01:17.784
Either way, the model should earn trust through testing.

13
00:01:17.784 --> 00:01:21.212
Evaluation should use the learner's own prompt sets.

14
00:01:21.212 --> 00:01:27.231
Try representative requests, compare outputs, note failures, and choose based on evidence.

15
00:01:27.231 --> 00:01:33.554
A local AI workflow is strongest when model selection is based on actual use, not reputation alone.

16
00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:38.811
Keep notes about why a model was accepted, rejected, or reserved for a narrow task.
